<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Glubb</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1897–1986</span> · Also known as Glubb Pasha, John Bagot Glubb</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Glubb, known as Glubb Pasha, was a British officer who commanded the Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a> of Transjordan and then Jordan from 1939 to 1956. He recruited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bedouin">Bedouin</a> into the desert patrol and made the Legion the most effective Arab army in the 1948 Arab-Israeli War. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hussein-of-jordan">King Hussein</a> dismissed him in 1956 amid rising Arab nationalism, and he later wrote many books on Arab history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-glubb.jpg" alt="John Glubb" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Willem van de Poll · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Glubb_Pasha_(1953).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
